.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# student data exports — contain names/mobiles/emails; never push these to a
# shared repo. Analytics/registration workbooks live locally only.
*.xlsx
/attempted_details_round1/

# student data exports — contain names/mobiles/emails; never push these to a shared repo
*.csv

# The college sends timetables and panel allocations as PDFs, and they carry the
# same names, roll numbers and mobile numbers the workbooks do (§8.10). /data/ is
# the working folder those land in — keep the whole folder out, not just the PDFs,
# so the next format someone drops in there is covered too.
*.pdf
/data/

# Raw photo drop folder for the "What We Offer" section — originals only.
# The 13 certification files alone are 162MB (6000x4000 each) and git keeps
# every blob forever, so these must never be committed. The curated, web-sized
# set the site actually loads is built from them by hand into
# public/assets/images/vvitu/whatweoffer/ (~1MB total) and IS committed.
public/assets/images/vvitu/WhatweOffer/

# Resume bundles pulled from the registration form (Drive uploads). Same PII as
# the workbooks: names, roll numbers, contact details. The PDFs themselves are
# already covered by *.pdf above; this covers the archive we hand to the team.
*.zip

# Database backups. A dump of vvitu_registrations and vvitu_hostel_roster is
# every student's name, roll number, email, mobile and interview remarks in one
# file — the single most sensitive artefact this repo can produce (§8.10).
# Never commit one; hand it over out of band like the .env.local credentials.
/backups/
